Heintzelman"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Joseph Hooker and Philip Kearny; deployed behind and south of Keyes’s advance"}]]}],["$","div","Commander, IV Corps; south of the Chickahominy-Erasmus D. Keyes",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Commander, IV Corps; south of the Chickahominy"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Erasmus D. Keyes"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Silas Casey in the forward position and Darius N. Couch in support along the Williamsburg Road"}]]}],["$","div","Commander, V Corps; right wing and Hanover expedition-Fitz John Porter",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Commander, V Corps; right wing and Hanover expedition"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Fitz John Porter"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"George W. Morell’s division and George Sykes’s division; Morell and attached troops fought at Hanover Court House"}]]}],["$","div","Commander, VI Corps; north of the Chickahominy-William B. Franklin",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Commander, VI Corps; north of the Chickahominy"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"William B. Franklin"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"William F. Smith and Henry W. Slocum; held the center-right portion of the northern wing"}]]}],["$","div","Commander, Department of the Rappahannock-Irvin McDowell",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Commander, Department of the Rappahannock"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Irvin McDowell"}],["$","small",null,{"children":"Expected to march south from Fredericksburg but diverted toward operations against Jackson before joining McClellan"}]]}]]]}],["$","section","Confederacy",{"className":"command-column #9a3d32","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Confederacy"}],[["$","div","President and commander in chief-Jefferson Davis",{"className":"command-entry","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"President and commander in chief"}],"$L1